processing-graph-taps = FIR taps (odd length)
processing-graph-add-profile = Add source noise range (initially 0–1 s)
processing-graph-mix-help = Inputs are aligned on the source timeline and summed with these gains, mute and solo settings. No hidden normalization or limiter. Disconnect a lane before removing it. Lane indices below start at zero.
processing-graph-add-lane = Add mix input
processing-graph-remove-lane = Remove last mix input
processing-graph-model-help = Backend and model are selected by this node’s manifest and Python environment, not global defaults. Supply a prepared MossFormer2 / NSNet2 / DeepFilterNet3 speech manifest or Kim Mel-band RoFormer / HTDemucs separation manifest as appropriate. A path is not proof of installed readiness. Errors are reported without algorithm, channel or sample-rate fallback.
processing-graph-offline = Offline
processing-graph-realtime = Real-time
processing-graph-hybrid = Hybrid
processing-graph-mode-help = Auto prioritizes exact-quality real-time execution, then a useful hybrid boundary, then offline rendering; the actual mode is shown with the run. Explicit real-time and hybrid modes reject unsupported plans. Runs capture an immutable graph revision. Preview computes only the selected output’s ancestors. Apply edited fields before running.
processing-graph-preview = Run selected output
processing-graph-run = Run graph output
processing-graph-result-older = This result’s audio graph differs from the current edited graph. Moving nodes alone does not change audio. Editing never alters captured results or an active run.
